The way I'm reading this is that with this change, all the stuff done in `test/` in this PR can be dropped.  Did I read that wrong?

I can confirm that these changes allow the entire test suite to pass against the 3.0.0 FIPS provider.

@t8m, I made a small change to the detection of the 3.0.0 FIPS provider -- the check routine doesn't return a Boolean, can also return a failure code.

I've also set the comments to a standard format: `FIPS(3.0.0): <reason> #issue` which should help us eventually remove them.

